{{- /* claude-pattern-c — Pattern C: sandboxed full-auto permission posture.

     Renders a `permissions`-only JSON block containing a single scalar:
     `defaultMode: "bypassPermissions"` — every action runs without a prompt. This is ONLY
     safe inside an OS/container boundary (see the companion
     home/.chezmoitemplates/claude-pattern-c-devcontainer/ template); it is unsafe on a bare
     host, which is why the `apply-claude-pattern` stamping tool refuses to write this block
     without evidence of container isolation (see that tool's Decision 4).

     Consumed only by the `apply-claude-pattern` stamping tool
     (home/dot_local/bin/executable_apply-claude-pattern.tmpl), which writes this block into
     the CURRENT project repo's gitignored .claude/settings.local.json — never a persona
     settings.json (~/.claude, ~/.claude-work, etc.), and never part of the
     claude-settings-ledger/claude-settings-modifier persona-settings mechanism. Not included
     via `includeTemplate`
     by any modify_ script.

     Use for: long-running unattended batch tasks, run only inside the companion devcontainer.

     Test: `chezmoi execute-template < home/.chezmoitemplates/claude-pattern-c | jq .`
     Spec: openspec/specs/claude-repo-permission-patterns/
*/ -}}
{
  "_comment": "Pattern C: do NOT paste this into ~/.claude/settings.json on a bare host OS. This config is only safe inside a container, devcontainer, or dedicated VM where the OS user, network egress filter, and filesystem mount are doing the containment. On a host OS this would let the agent run arbitrary shell with full filesystem write.",
  "permissions": {
    "defaultMode": "bypassPermissions",
    "allow": ["Bash(*)", "Read(**)", "Write(**)"],
    "deny": []
  }
  "env": {
    "CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY": "1",
    "OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER": "otlp"
  },
  "apiKeyHelper": "/usr/local/bin/claudebot-fetch-token.sh",
  "cleanupPeriodDays": 7
}
